IMPORT prelude

-- Rubber Industry Act 1992 (Singapore) -- who needs a rubber licence (ss 2, 3), when the Board must refuse one (s 4), renewal
-- (s 6), the licensee's inspection duty (s 10), the Board's own sanctions and the stay pending appeal (s 11), the two appeal routes
-- and their deadlines (ss 7, 12), the criminal penalties (ss 3(3), 8, 10(3), 20, 23) and officers of a company (s 24).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/RIA1992.txt. The deposit says it "incorporates all
-- amendments up to and including 1 December 2021 and comes into operation on 31 December 2021". The latest amending Act annotated in
-- the body is 40/2019 (at s 13(1)). The ARRANGEMENT OF SECTIONS at the top of the deposit is one number out of step with the body
-- (it numbers "Short title" as 2); this encoding follows the body.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0117 in ../../../requirements.jsonl: Tier 2 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. It asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked a sharper
-- question yet. SCOPED to the licensing regime as a trader meets it. Not encoded: the Board's market and arbitration powers (s 14),
-- Ministerial directions (s 15), entry and seizure (ss 16, 17), immunity (s 18), the Rubber Fund (s 19), prosecution machinery
-- (ss 21, 22, 25), the Appeal Tribunal's constitution (s 13), regulations and by-laws (ss 26, 27), and the content of any licence
-- conditions or fees (prescribed by regulations that were not retrieved). The s 28 exemption is a bare input.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Rubber Industry Act 1992 -- licensing`

DECLARE Activity IS ONE OF
    `packing rubber for export`
    `shipping rubber for export`
    `manufacturing technically specified rubber`
    `dealing in rubber`
    `treating rubber`
    `storing rubber`
    `trading rubber futures contracts`
    `selling rubber gloves`

§§ `2, 3 -- who needs a licence`

-- s 2: "deal" means "to broke in, purchase or sell rubber but does not include the purchase, sale or brokerage of rubber by means of
-- a commodity futures contract"; "rubber" means "marketable rubber prepared from the leaves, bark or latex of any rubber plant, but
-- does not include any manufactured article made wholly or partly of rubber"; "treat" means "to subject to any process whatsoever".
-- s 3(1): a person "must not (a) pack rubber for export; (b) ship rubber for export; (c) manufacture or otherwise produce
-- technically specified rubber; or (d) deal in, treat or store rubber, unless the person is for the time being the holder of a valid
-- licence ... authorising the person to do so or is a person employed by the holder of such a licence."
GIVEN `the activity` IS AN Activity
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the activity needs a licence` IF
    CONSIDER `the activity`
    WHEN `trading rubber futures contracts` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `selling rubber gloves` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 3(3): contravening (1) -- fine not exceeding $25,000 or imprisonment not exceeding 2 years or both.
-- s 3(4): (1) "does not apply to a person who ships rubber for export if the person is the holder of a licence issued ... under the
-- provisions of the Malaysian Rubber Board (Incorporation) Act 1996"; (5): only "so long as reciprocal arrangements exist between
-- Singapore and Malaysia". The Malaysian licence covers SHIPPING only, not packing, dealing or storing.
-- s 28: the Board may, with the Minister's approval, exempt any person from all or any provisions (a bare input here).
DECLARE Trader HAS
    `activity` IS AN Activity
    `holds a licence authorising the activity` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is employed by such a licensee` IS A BOOLEAN
    `holds a Malaysian rubber shipping licence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `reciprocal arrangements with Malaysia exist` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is exempted under s 28` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `t` IS A Trader
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Malaysian licence exception applies` IF
        `t`'s `activity` EQUALS `shipping rubber for export`
    AND `t`'s `holds a Malaysian rubber shipping licence`
    AND `t`'s `reciprocal arrangements with Malaysia exist`

GIVEN `t` IS A Trader
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the trader commits the s 3 offence` IF
        `the activity needs a licence` (`t`'s `activity`)
    AND (NOT `t`'s `holds a licence authorising the activity`)
    AND (NOT `t`'s `is employed by such a licensee`)
    AND (NOT `the Malaysian licence exception applies` `t`)
    AND (NOT `t`'s `is exempted under s 28`)

§§ `4 -- grant and mandatory refusal`

-- s 4(2): the Board "may grant a licence for a period of one year at a time, with or without conditions, or refuse".
-- s 4(3): the Board "must refuse" if (a) satisfactory evidence has not been produced that the applicant is "a fit and proper person";
-- (b) the applicant or, if a company, "any of its officers holding a managerial or executive position" has been convicted of "any
-- offence involving dishonesty, fraud or moral turpitude"; or (c) "the Board considers it in the public interest to do so".
-- s 4(4): a person "who is not an incorporated person may not be licensed" unless registered under a registered business name under
-- the Business Names Registration Act 2014.
-- s 4(5): every licensee must pay the prescribed annual fee (amount not in the Act).
DECLARE Applicant HAS
    `produced satisfactory evidence of being fit and proper` IS A BOOLEAN
    `applicant or a managerial officer has a dishonesty conviction` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Board considers refusal in the public interest` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is incorporated` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is registered under a business name` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `a` IS AN Applicant
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the licence cannot be granted` IF
        (NOT `a`'s `produced satisfactory evidence of being fit and proper`)
    OR  `a`'s `applicant or a managerial officer has a dishonesty conviction`
    OR  `a`'s `the Board considers refusal in the public interest`
    OR  ((NOT `a`'s `is incorporated`) AND (NOT `a`'s `is registered under a business name`))

GIVETH A NUMBER
`the licence term in years` MEANS 1

§§ `6 -- renewal`

-- s 6(1): "An application to renew a licence must be made to the Board one month before the expiry of the licence." The text says
-- "one month before", not "at least one month before"; this encoding reads it as AT LEAST one month (an inference).
-- s 6(2): the Board MAY refuse to renew if of the opinion that the holder "has contravened or failed to comply with any of the
-- conditions of the licence or the provisions of this Act or any regulations or by-laws"; (3) it must first notify in writing and
-- give "a reasonable opportunity of being heard".
GIVEN `months before expiry` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the renewal application is in time` IF `months before expiry` AT LEAST 1

GIVEN `the Board thinks the holder contravened` IS A BOOLEAN, `the holder was notified and heard` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Board may refuse renewal` IF `the Board thinks the holder contravened` AND `the holder was notified and heard`

§§ `10 -- inspection of premises`

-- s 10(1): every licensee must allow inspection of premises where it carries on "the business of packing rubber for export or dealing
-- in, treating or storing rubber or manufacturing technically specified rubber". SHIPPING for export is not in the list, though s 9
-- (display of licence) does include it. (3): failing without lawful excuse to produce books, documents or rubber -- $5,000 or
-- 6 months or both.
GIVEN `the activity` IS AN Activity
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the premises are open to s 10 inspection` IF
    CONSIDER `the activity`
    WHEN `packing rubber for export` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `manufacturing technically specified rubber` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `dealing in rubber` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `treating rubber` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `storing rubber` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `11 -- the Board's own sanctions`

-- s 11(1): if the Board is satisfied that a licensee "is contravening, or has contravened and is likely again to contravene", any
-- condition, the Act, regulations or by-laws, it may by written notice "and without any compensation": (a) revoke; (b) suspend;
-- (c) on suspension, prohibit renewal; (d) "impose a fine not exceeding $25,000, which is recoverable in the same manner as a
-- judgment debt"; (e) require a deposit or bank guarantee "not exceeding $25,000"; (f) warn; (g) order payment of "a sum not
-- exceeding $5,000 to cover the costs incurred by the Board".
-- (2): "The Board must not proceed under subsection (1) without first giving the licensee a reasonable opportunity of being heard."
DECLARE Decision IS ONE OF
    `refusal of a licence`
    `new licence conditions`
    `refusal to renew`
    `revocation`
    `suspension`
    `a Board fine`
    `a security deposit`
    `a warning`
    `a costs order`

GIVEN `is contravening` IS A BOOLEAN, `has contravened` IS A BOOLEAN, `is likely to contravene again` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `was given a hearing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Board may act under s 11` IF
        `was given a hearing`
    AND (`is contravening` OR (`has contravened` AND `is likely to contravene again`))

GIVEN `the decision` IS A Decision, `amount` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the amount is within s 11` IF
    CONSIDER `the decision`
    WHEN `a Board fine` THEN `amount` AT MOST 25000
    WHEN `a security deposit` THEN `amount` AT MOST 25000
    WHEN `a costs order` THEN `amount` AT MOST 5000
    OTHERWISE `amount` EQUALS 0

-- s 11(4): "Execution of any decision of the Board conveyed in the notice ... must be stayed pending the expiry of the period within
-- which a notice of appeal under section 12 may be given or the decision on such appeal". The 14-day period is s 12(2); an
-- extension of time by the Tribunal (s 12(7)) is not modelled.
GIVEN `days since the notice was received` IS A NUMBER, `an appeal was lodged` IS A BOOLEAN, `the appeal was decided` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the s 11 decision may be executed` IF
    IF `an appeal was lodged`
    THEN `the appeal was decided`
    ELSE `days since the notice was received` GREATER THAN 14

§§ `7, 12 -- appeals`

DECLARE Forum IS ONE OF
    `the Minister`
    `the Appeal Tribunal`

-- s 7: a person aggrieved by a decision "under section 4, 5 or 6 may, within one month of being notified of the decision, appeal
-- ... to the Minister whose decision is final".
-- s 12(1), (2): a person aggrieved by a decision "under section 11(1)" may appeal to the Appeal Tribunal; written notice with grounds
-- "within 14 days of the receipt ... of the notice", copy served on the Board; (5) the Tribunal's decision is "final and conclusive";
-- (7) the Tribunal "may extend any limit of time fixed for the giving of a notice of appeal". No extension is provided for s 7.
GIVEN `the decision` IS A Decision
GIVETH A Forum
`the appeal lies to` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the decision`
    WHEN `refusal of a licence` THEN `the Minister`
    WHEN `new licence conditions` THEN `the Minister`
    WHEN `refusal to renew` THEN `the Minister`
    OTHERWISE `the Appeal Tribunal`

GIVEN `the decision` IS A Decision, `days since notice` IS A NUMBER, `still within one month of notice` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the Tribunal extended time` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the appeal is in time` IF
    IF `the appeal lies to` `the decision` EQUALS `the Minister`
    THEN `still within one month of notice`
    ELSE (`days since notice` AT MOST 14) OR `the Tribunal extended time`

§§ `3(3), 8, 10(3), 20, 23 -- criminal penalties`

-- s 3(3) unlicensed activity: $25,000 or 2 years or both. s 8 wilfully false or misleading statement in an application for grant or
-- renewal: $2,000 or 6 months or both. s 10(3) failing without lawful excuse to produce books, documents or rubber: $5,000 or
-- 6 months or both. s 20 obstructing or hindering the Chairperson, chief executive or an officer or agent: $5,000 or 6 months or
-- both. s 23(1) an offence under the Act or regulations "for which no penalty is expressly provided": $5,000 or 3 months or both.
-- s 22: no court may try an offence without the Public Prosecutor's consent.
DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `operating without a licence`
    `a false statement in an application`
    `failing to produce books or rubber`
    `obstructing a Board officer`
    `an offence with no express penalty`

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `operating without a licence` THEN 25000
    WHEN `a false statement in an application` THEN 2000
    OTHERWISE 5000

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in months` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `operating without a licence` THEN 24
    WHEN `an offence with no express penalty` THEN 3
    OTHERWISE 6

-- s 23(2): the Board may compound an offence "which is prescribed as a compoundable offence by collecting ... a sum not exceeding
-- $2,000"; (3) the offences are prescribed by regulations (not retrieved).
GIVEN `the offence is prescribed as compoundable` IS A BOOLEAN, `sum` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the offence may be compounded for the sum` IF `the offence is prescribed as compoundable` AND `sum` AT MOST 2000

§§ `24 -- officers of a company`

-- s 24: where an offence is committed by a body corporate and "proved to have been committed with the consent or connivance of, or to
-- be attributable to an act or default on the part of, a director, manager, secretary or other similar officer", that person "as
-- well as the body corporate" is guilty.
GIVEN `the company committed the offence` IS A BOOLEAN, `with the officer's consent or connivance` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `attributable to the officer's act or default` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the officer is also guilty` IF
        `the company committed the offence`
    AND (`with the officer's consent or connivance` OR `attributable to the officer's act or default`)
